{
 "result": "maze.py is a flat-bytearray BFS with a sentinel border. It reads stdin, finds S and E with bytes.find, and expands level by level, marking visited cells as '#'. It returns the distance at the first E it reaches, or -1. It passes all three public samples (2008, -1, 78) and is registered as the baseline at 3.43816 with noise 8.3%. I'm resting rather than spending the last ~47 energy on a variant, since a win beyond noise needs a clear speedup and the remaining energy would likely not cover the thinking cost.",
